35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some really important stuff! The bills are all over the place—February was almost 30,000 yen, but August was only 9,100! It's a huge difference! Also, some payments were really late because people were confused about the amounts.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The volatility is significant. The gap between February and August confirms that seasonal fluctuations are a major factor. We cannot rely on a simple average if we want to avoid sudden financial strain during the winter.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that the ""magic tricks"" aren't so magic! The other house spends forty minutes just reading meters and doing math by hand! And that template takes forever because you have to type in every single invoice!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems the ""magic"" is just manual labor, Rin. As for the logs, they're a disaster. Payments are late and people are questioning the amounts. It's exactly as I suspected: the current system is a breeding ground for resentment.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, you're right. The logs show that payments were delayed multiple times because people were confused or questioned the amounts. It's clear that the current way we handle money is creating tension between us.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, it's so sad that people were confused! I don't want anyone to feel stressed about money. But look at those winter bills! If February is that high, we really need a plan that doesn't surprise us in the cold!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, exactly. The winter spike is the primary risk. Furthermore, I found that installing sub-meters would cost 34,000 yen per room plus annual maintenance. We must consider if such a high upfront cost is justifiable for the sake of precision.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that's so expensive! But the real scary part is the time! If the other house takes forty minutes every month and that template is a total slog, who's going to do all that work? I don't want anyone's whole evening to disappear!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, forty minutes is a small price to pay to avoid a house full of people wondering who is paying for whose heater. The real cost is the three weeks we wasted just arguing over the newcomers' shares. We're currently paying for incompetence.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, it wasn't just incompetence; it was a lack of a clear system. The fact that we had to write off part of the cost just to end the argument shows how fragile our current agreement is. We need a method that removes the need for negotiation.","{""words"":47,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that sounds so stressful! I hate the idea of us arguing over money. But @Ryuji, if sub-meters are too expensive, maybe we can just be honest about how we use things? I don't want anyone feeling like they have to freeze just to save money!","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, honesty is subjective and doesn't solve the financial volatility. We need a system that accounts for the winter spikes without creating a deficit. However, spending over 100,000 yen on sub-meters seems irrational given our current budget.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, but if we don't have meters, we're back to that scary math! If the person doing the bills has to spend hours every month answering questions and typing in invoices, they'll get super grumpy! We need a way that's fast!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your obsession with ""fast"" is just a desire to avoid the inevitable. Whether it takes ten minutes or an hour, the math doesn't change. The real issue is that we're splitting bills based on a ghost agreement from when only three of us lived here.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, exactly. We are clinging to an outdated arrangement that no longer fits our reality. The friction we've seen in the logs isn't just about the math; it's about the lack of a transparent, updated agreement for five people.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, you're so right! We need a fresh start that everyone agrees on. I just hope we can be open about how we actually use the heating and water, so nobody feels they have to suffer in silence!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, openness is not a substitute for a structured plan. We must prioritize a system that is both financially predictable and administratively sustainable. We cannot afford a solution that is either too expensive to implement or too tedious to maintain.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that's exactly what I'm worried about! If the system is too tedious, the person in charge will just get exhausted. Let's make sure we pick something that doesn't turn into a giant chore for one person!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, you're worrying about a few minutes of paperwork while the house is practically simmering with silent grudges. Let's stop pretending this is about ""chores"" and admit it's about who's paying for whom. I'm ready to see the options.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree with Shunichi. The delays and the write-offs we've seen are symptoms of a deeper problem. If we don't address the tension caused by these payments now, no amount of ""fast math"" will fix the atmosphere in this house.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
