60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A sounds so helpful! If we agree on a set amount for each season, we won't have those scary surprises in February, and nobody will feel pressured to freeze just to keep the bill down!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A is the most rational choice. It addresses the seasonal volatility I found in the statements, ensuring that the winter spikes don't become a sudden financial burden. It provides the predictability we need to budget effectively.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option A sounds okay, but what about the end of the year? If we have to do a giant reconciliation then, won't that be a total nightmare of typing in invoices and math? I'm worried it'll be a huge chore!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, you're terrified of a little arithmetic once a year, yet you're fine with the current chaos. Option A just kicks the can down the road. It doesn't solve the core issue: who is actually using the energy?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, you're right that it doesn't track individual usage, but Option A removes the monthly friction. If we stop arguing over every single invoice, we might actually start speaking to each other normally again.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, exactly! If we stop worrying about the exact yen every month, we can just relax and be friends! Plus, it means we can be honest about needing the heat in winter without feeling guilty!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, while friendship is a pleasant byproduct, the primary goal is financial stability. Option B is out of the question; the installation costs I found are far too high to be a reasonable investment for this household.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, I agree that B is too expensive! But @Misaki, if we do Option A, who has to do that big year-end math? If it's like that template I saw, it'll take forever! That's not fair to the person doing it!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your fear of a spreadsheet is not a valid reason to maintain a system where people are subsidizing each other. Option C is the only one that is honest about our current situation, even if it's simple.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, Option C is simple, but it's exactly what we're doing now. The logs show that monthly recalculations and queries are where the tension peaks. We need a system that reduces the frequency of these confrontations.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, you're so right! Option C just keeps us in this cycle of confusion and late payments. I really think Option A is the best because it lets us breathe and feel cozy without the guilt!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, Option C is a recipe for continued instability. It ignores the seasonal spikes that make winter payments feel like a second rent. Option A is the only choice that provides the predictability necessary for a sustainable budget.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, @Ryuji, I want to be cozy too! But if we do Option A, we have to make sure the year-end math isn't a monster! If we can find a way to make it fast, then I'm for it!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, you're still treating this like a game of ""how to avoid work."" The real monster is the resentment of paying for someone else's luxury. Option A is just a mask; Option C is the only honest, if blunt, approach.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, honesty without a system is just an invitation to argue. Option C is the blunt approach that has already damaged our relationships. Option A prioritizes our peace of mind by minimizing the monthly conflict. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm so glad we're all talking this through! I really want us to feel happy and warm in our home, and Option A is the only one that lets us do that without stress. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is the only logical choice. It eliminates the financial shock of winter spikes and avoids the prohibitive costs of sub-meters. It is the most sustainable and predictable system for our budget. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Misaki, @Ryuji, you've convinced me! As long as we all help out with the year-end math so it doesn't swallow one person's whole evening, I'm in! Let's go with the cozy plan! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"You're all choosing a comfortable lie over an uncomfortable truth. Option A is just a way to pretend the resentment isn't there until December. But if you're all that desperate for a facade of peace, I'll stop fighting. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. While it doesn't solve every individual's usage concern, it stops the monthly cycle of accusations and delays. For the sake of our relationships and a peaceful home, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
